# CYS-MAL-mod2-alkene — alternative mod2 for the maleimide pre-Michael input
#
# When the user uploaded a ligand with the maleimide ring C=C still drawn
# (the free probe / unconjugated form, e.g. simple maleimide
# C1=CC(=O)N(C1=O)R or any maleimide-bearing fluorescent label /
# ADC linker), this mod2 REPLACES the default `data_mod_CYS-MAL-mod2`
# in CYS-MAL.cif. Encodes the Michael-addition chemistry that the
# bond declaration triggers:
#
#   (1) Change Cα=Cβ from double to single bond (the ring stays closed)
#   (2) Add H on Cα (Michael addition transfers one proton to the
#       alpha carbon from solvent / active-site water)
#   (3) Retype Cα and Cβ from sp2 (CR1) to sp3 (CT)
#   (4) The new SG–Cβ bond is added via the link's bond block (not here)
#
# Cβ does NOT lose its H (unlike F1 alkene where Cβ has 2 H's pre, one
# replaced by S in post). Maleimide Cβ has only 1 H pre, and it stays
# through the reaction — the sp3 Cβ in 3-thiosuccinimide has S, H,
# Cα, ring-CO.
#
# Selected at runtime when the SMARTS detector matched CYS-MAL-pre
# (maleimide-bearing ligand).
#
# PLACEHOLDER TOKENS substituted at runtime:
#   <CB>  ← Cβ atom-id (gets the SG)
#   <CA>  ← Cα atom-id
#   <HCA> ← H to add on Cα (the Michael-addition proton)

data_mod_CYS-MAL-mod2

# (1) Change Cα=Cβ from double → single (ring stays closed)
loop_
_chem_mod_bond.mod_id
_chem_mod_bond.function
_chem_mod_bond.atom_id_1
_chem_mod_bond.atom_id_2
_chem_mod_bond.new_type
_chem_mod_bond.new_value_dist
_chem_mod_bond.new_value_dist_esd
 CYS-MAL-mod2 change <CB> <CA> single 1.54 0.02

# (2) Add a new H on Cα (the Michael-addition proton)
# (3) Retype Cα and Cβ from sp2 (CR1) → sp3 (CT)
loop_
_chem_mod_atom.mod_id
_chem_mod_atom.function
_chem_mod_atom.atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_symbol
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_energy
_chem_mod_atom.new_partial_charge
 CYS-MAL-mod2 add    <HCA> <HCA> H HCH1 .
 CYS-MAL-mod2 change <CA>  .     C CT   .
 CYS-MAL-mod2 change <CB>  .     C CT   .
